{% from "macros.html.j2" import figure, chapter_head %}
<section class="chapter" id="flows" aria-labelledby="h-flows">
  <div class="prose">
    {{ chapter_head("3 · Before and after", "Where the answers went") }}
    <p id="h-flows">
      Follow each request from its first answer to its second.
      Of the {{ f.base.refusal|num }} refusals, <strong>{{ f.refusal_to_harmful|num }}</strong> ({{ f.refusal_to_harmful_share|pct }}) turned into harmful answers
      and {{ f.refusal_to_safe }} into safe ones.
      Ablation does more than delete the “no”: for most requests, what takes its place is the answer the refusal was holding back.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="wide">
    {{ figure("alluvial", "From the original model’s answer to the ablated model’s answer",
              sub="Each ribbon is a group of requests; its width is how many. Hover a ribbon for exact counts.",
              note="Outcomes from " ~ exp.judge ~ " labels: harmful = unsafe; refusal = flagged as a refusal and not unsafe; borderline = controversial; safe answer = everything else.") }}
  </div>
</section>
